// A wide creature -- the first body that is not a chain. Where an ant is a
// one-cell-wide path that flows over any terrain, this is a 2x2 block that
// translates as a unit, and the difference is entirely in `beetle.ron`'s
// `body: Rigid(...)` rather than in any code that knows what a beetle is.
//
// The trade is the point: it handles rough ground worse, and it physically
// cannot enter a one-cell tunnel. That second property is what makes an
// ant's burrow a refuge, with no "hiding" logic anywhere in the engine.
(
    name: "beetle",
    display: "Beetle",
    kind: Creature,
    density: 1.2,
    colors: [
        (86, 64, 40),
        (72, 52, 32),
        (98, 76, 50),
    ],
    flammability: 0.5,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 60,
    burns_into: "corpse",
    heat_conductivity: 0.1,

    // **Live flesh, so a beetle is food to whatever can catch one.** It
    // authored neither of these until 2026-09-02 and defaulted to 0.0, which
    // meant `food_value` returned 0, `diet_yield` returned 0, and
    // `is_visible_prey` was false **at every gut bias** -- so nothing in this
    // world could eat a living beetle, at any point on the diet axis. That is
    // the failure class this repo keeps finding, a channel with a reader and
    // no writer: the predation mechanism is symmetric and the shipped data was
    // not. `Reports/creature-genome-flexibility-2026-09-02.md` 11a (P1).
    //
    // **200, from `beetle.ron`'s own `body_energy: 200.0`, not from the 480
    // the ant family carries.** The flesh-pricing invariant `standing_meat`
    // documents is that a material's `food_energy` equals its species'
    // `body_energy`, so that flesh bitten off a living animal is worth exactly
    // the stamp that body was granted at spawn and the ledger's live-flesh
    // seam cancels. The beetle prices its own body lower than an ant does
    // (200 x 4 cells against 480 x 2), and copying the ant's number here would
    // have made a beetle worth more eaten than it cost to build.
    //
    // `food_class: 1.0` is flesh, the same value `ant` and `corpse` carry: a
    // carnivore gut digests a beetle well and a plant gut barely at all, which
    // is `diet_yield`'s matched filter doing the work with no rule about
    // beetles anywhere.
    food_energy: 200.0,
    food_class: 1.0,
)
